From: gsdali <51393997+gsdali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:06:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet builds a
 fillet wider than its face

A fillet whose radius is above the width of the face it sits on (r > 4 on a 4 mm face) has no
start solution in the stripe builder: the contact line on the far face lies outside the face (#1177).

When Compute() fails for a single straight edge between two planar rectangles at a right angle,
Build now cuts the shape by the prism of the region between the arc and the faces. The arc stays
tangent to the face that lasts and passes through the far edge of the face that runs out (the
pivot), or through both far edges when both run out. The cut must give one valid closed solid and
remove exactly the section area times the edge length; otherwise the failure stands.

The same cut serves the contours of the opposite-edge fallback, so two fillets that both run out
of face are built as the intersection of their pivot results.

TKFillet links TKPrim, which it already reaches through TKBO.
